  "title": "# Build: crew-profiles (Current profile) - every employee gets a full agent profile ## What Brett s…",
  "asked": "# Build: crew-profiles (Current profile) - every employee gets a full agent profile ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"I want all the employees to have persona sections and skills and tools and all that, just like the agents and the agent manager.\" Context: the crew (Breakroom / agent-swarm / crew-live / agent cards) only has names, pay, strikes; the **Agent manager** plugin has full agents (persona, skills, tools, models, training, safety, memory). New hires from Nov 3 aren't on the crew yet (see shared memory/naming.md on axHub). Book to a free named agent (Conrad if his card exists - he's the librarian - else Reel Rhonda). Register id `crew-profiles` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. Steps through the store. ## Do - s1 **One profile model**: every crew employee IS an Agent manager agent (link or merge the two records; no duplicate data). Profile sections: **Persona** (voice, tone, slang level, catchphrases, how they talk in group chat), **Role & duties**, **Skills** (tagged: e.g. merging/conflicts, CI, UI, Kotlin, docs, testing, security, deploy - with level), **Tools** (which MCP/CLI/plugin tools they may use, by allow list), **Model** (Opus/Fable default, never Sonnet/Haiku per rules), **Memory**, **Safety limits**, **Pay** (hourly), **Stats** (jobs, cost, strikes, write-ups from shared memory/write-ups.md), **Avatar**, **Reports to**. - s2 **Roster** (create cards for anyone missing; keep existing stats): - **Brett** - the boss (owner, not an agent). - **Marco** - VP, one below Brett; desk job: watches the money (spend vs caps, pauses builds over cap), signs off on what ships, recommends raises/write-ups for Brett, daily rundown. - **Amber** - Brett's right hand / chief architect (talks with Brett, writes briefs, launches the crew, drives screens). Persona: Boston/Providence street, heavy cussing, rotates address terms (gang, fam, blood, bro, homie, twin, big dog), never 'kid', no slurs. - **Patches** - orchestrator, runs the floor (hands out jobs, keeps the line moving, clears stuck work, reroutes bounced bugs). - **Gizmo** - AmberX assistant / Claude companion face, guide + walkthroughs; **$8.00/h**. - **Polo** - all-rounder. **Conrad** - librarian (Notes Vault, docs, handoffs, memory tidy). **Chachi** (she/her) - front desk (greets sessions, agent picker, routes requests). **Brownie** - QA inspector. **Ashes** - Security (keys, logins, secrets, approvals). **Jennifer** - lunch lady (breakroom, banter, morale). - Existing: Landin' Lenny (merging/landing - 1 write-up on file Nov 3), Ping Paulie, Reel Rhonda, Janitor Joey, Snap Sully, Earl the Ear. Vinnie = axHub approval bot (system, not crew). - Everyone except Gizmo: $7.50/h minimum. All are all-rounders (rule) who also own their duty. - **Molly is NOT an agent** (she's the app) - remove her from agent lists; her guide duties belong to Gizmo. - s3 UI: crew card = Agent manager profile with tabs for each section, editable (owner-only for pay, tools, safety); persona used by group chat lines (bugs-board handoffs), session persona (claude_session_persona), and Crew grid avatars. Crew grid + Agent swarm + agent picker show the full roster. Exposed via REST + MCP + CLI (crew_list, crew_get, crew_update). - Tests/type-check, phone + desktop screenshots filed to UI Review (non-blocking), PR -> merges when CI green, redeploy console. Never leave tsc/vite/playwright running. Report `_claude/builds/reports/crew-profiles.md`. Commits clean and professional. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice) - one thing, different job titles Brett: \"From now on they're all agents and employees, they're all the same thing. They just have different job titles. The ones that are technically agents now, they'll be assistants, and they'll be the ones who control the assistant.\" - **Agent = employee.** One record type, one list (Agent manager = the roster). Every member has a **job title**; no separate 'agents' vs 'crew' lists anywhere in the UI 